     271.80 = 1891.80. The two grand-total fields move TOGETHER, so BR-CO-16 (amount due =
     grand total, no prepaid/rounding) stays satisfied and the ONLY fired rule is BR-CO-15
     (fatal): the invoice total with VAT (BT-112) must equal total without VAT (BT-109) + total
     VAT (BT-110). Every mandatory BG group is intact and the per-breakdown VAT (BR-CO-14),
     line-sum (BR-CO-10) and tax-basis (BR-CO-13) arithmetic all still reconcile, so exactly one
     distinct fatal is isolated — distinct from the BR-CO-14 (synth-cii-bad-vat-mismatch),
     BR-S-02 (synth-cii-bad-missing-seller-vat) and BR-DE-2 (synth-cii-bad-xrechnung-nocontact)
     fatals the other bad-synth CII goldens pin.

     Arithmetic (all EUR):
       Line 1  Widget   qty 10 @ 100.00 = 1000.00, -50.00 line allowance -> BT-131 950.00 (19%)
       Line 2  Install  qty  5 @  80.00 =  400.00, +30.00 line charge     -> BT-131 430.00 (19%)
       Line 3  Manual   qty 12 @  25.00 =  300.00                          -> BT-131 300.00 ( 7%)
       Sum of line net amounts (BT-106)            = 950.00 + 430.00 + 300.00 = 1680.00
       Document allowance (BT-107, 19%)            = 100.00
       Document charge    (BT-108, 19%)            =  40.00
       19% breakdown basis = 950 + 430 - 100 + 40  = 1320.00 -> VAT 250.80
        7% breakdown basis = 300                    =  300.00 -> VAT  21.00
       Tax basis total (BT-109) = 1680 - 100 + 40   = 1620.00
       VAT total       (BT-110) = 250.80 + 21.00    =  271.80
       Grand total     (BT-112) SHOULD be 1891.80 but is OVERSTATED to 1991.80  <- BR-CO-15
       Amount due      (BT-115) moved in lockstep to 1991.80 (keeps BR-CO-16)   -->
